---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /
background: false
description: "Aydin Mohseni is a mathematical philosopher at Carnegie Mellon University who uses evolutionary game theory and Bayesian epistemology to study problems in AI safety and metascience."
---
{%- from "partials/macros.njk" import section, model, authorLine, verifyNote with context -%}
{#- The home page carries the argument, in the section order of docs/BRIEF.md: who, a live model,
    the research strands, talks, co-inquirers, influences, contact. Within a strand the order is
    danielherrmann.ca's: heading, essay, model with caption and "How it works", selected work,
    related ∃xProof AI programs. Content comes from src/_data; nothing here states a view of
    Aydin's that the data does not source. Anything the Research page marks data-verify is
    marked here too (verifyNote for works, the talk's own flag for talks). -#}
{%- set research = '/publications/' | url -%}

<section class="hero home-hero home-hero--intro" aria-labelledby="home-title">
  <img class="intro-photo" src="{{ '/assets/img/mohseni.jpg' | url }}" alt="Portrait of Aydin Mohseni" width="360" height="360">
  <div class="intro-text">
    <h1 id="home-title"><span class="visually-hidden">Aydin Mohseni, </span>Evolutionary game theorist, Bayesian epistemologist, and philosopher of science and of AI.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I am an Assistant Professor of <a href="https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/">Philosophy at Carnegie Mellon</a>, a core member of the <a href="https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/social-dynamics/">Institute for Complex Social Dynamics</a>, and co-director of <a class="xp" href="https://exproof.ai/">{{ "" | exproofName | safe }}</a> with <a href="https://www.danielherrmann.ca/">Daniel Herrmann</a>. I use evolutionary game theory and Bayesian epistemology to study problems in AI safety and metascience.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{% call section("", "dynamics") %}
<h2>Selection need not settle</h2>
<p data-verify="Draft in Aydin's voice; his to approve or rewrite.">Most of what I study, from scientific communities to AI systems, is a population of adaptive agents. Equilibrium analysis asks where such a population comes to rest. But selection and learning need not come to rest. The replicator dynamics, the simplest model of selection and also the limit of simple reinforcement learning, can wander forever, and four strategies are already enough. Below is that minimal case.</p>
{{ model("chaos",
  caption="The replicator dynamics for a four-strategy game. Each point of the tetrahedron is a population state. Started near the center, the orbit never settles: it folds into a strange attractor, and nearby starts drift apart. Drag to rotate.",
  number="1",
  options={ mode: "hero" },
  id="model-chaos",
  aspect="10 / 9") }}
{% endcall %}

{% call section("Constant co-inquirers", "coinquirers", wide=true) %}
<ul class="names">
  {%- for c in coinquirers %}{% if c.constant %}
  <li>{% if c.url %}<a href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.display }}</a>{% else %}{{ c.display }}{% endif %}<span class="d">
    {%- for slug in c.works %}{% set w = publications | findBySlug(slug) %}{% if w %}<a href="{{ research }}#pub-{{ w.slug }}">{{ w.title }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}</span></li>
  {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endcall %}

{%- for s in strands %}
{%- set n = loop.index + 1 %}
{% call section(s.title, "strand-" ~ s.slug) %}
<h2>{{ s.topics }}</h2>
{%- for para in s.essay.slice(0, 1) %}
<p{% if para.verify %} data-verify="{{ para.verify }}"{% endif %}>{{ para.text | linkPhrases(s.links, { slugBase: research, quote: true, people: coinquirers }) | safe }}</p>
{%- endfor %}
{{ model(s.model, caption=s.caption, number=n, options={}, id="model-" ~ s.model, aspect="16 / 10") }}
<details class="expand selected-work">
<summary>Selected work</summary>
<ul class="featured">
  {%- for slug in s.selected.slice(0, 3) %}
  {%- set w = publications | findBySlug(slug) %}
  {%- if w %}
  {%- set note = verifyNote(w) | string | trim %}
  <li{% if note | length %} data-verify="{{ note }}"{% endif %}><span class="t"><a href="{{ research }}#pub-{{ w.slug }}">{{ w.title }}</a></span><span class="d">
    {%- if w.status == "published" and w.venue %}<i>{{ w.venue }}</i>, {{ "forthcoming" if w.forthcoming else w.year }}.
    {%- elif w.status == "under-review" %}{{ "Revise and resubmit." if w.revise_and_resubmit else "Under review." }}
    {%- else %}In progress.{% endif %}
    {%- set others = w.authors | coauthors %}
    {%- if others.length %} With {{ authorLine(others, coinquirers, true) }}.{% endif %}</span></li>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
</details>
{%- if s.exproof and s.exproof.length %}
{#- As on danielherrmann.ca: a card for the group after the AI safety strand. -#}
<a class="xp-card" href="https://exproof.ai/">
  <span class="xp-mark"><span class="exists" aria-hidden="true">&exist;</span><span class="visually-hidden">E</span>xProof AI</span>
  <span class="xp-line">The research group I co-direct with Daniel Herrmann, searching for a path to safe AI, if one exists.</span>
  <span class="xp-go">exproof.ai &rarr;</span>
</a>
{%- endif %}
{% endcall %}
{%- endfor %}

{%- set upcomingTalks = talks | upcoming | soonestFirst %}
{%- set pastTalks = talks | past %}
{% call section("Recent and upcoming talks", "talks") %}
<ul class="featured talks-list">
  {%- for t in upcomingTalks %}
  <li{% if t.verify %} data-verify="{{ t.verify_note }}"{% endif %}><span class="t">{% if t.paper_slug %}<a href="{{ research }}#pub-{{ t.paper_slug }}">{{ t.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ t.title }}{% endif %}</span><span class="d"><span class="tag">Upcoming</span> {{ t.venue }}, {{ t.city }}, {{ t.date | formatDate }}.</span></li>
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- for t in pastTalks.slice(0, (3 - upcomingTalks.length) if upcomingTalks.length < 3 else 0) %}
  <li{% if t.verify %} data-verify="{{ t.verify_note }}"{% endif %}><span class="t">{% if t.paper_slug %}<a href="{{ research }}#pub-{{ t.paper_slug }}">{{ t.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ t.title }}{% endif %}</span><span class="d">{{ t.venue }}, {{ t.city }}, {{ t.date | formatDate }}.{% if t.video %} <a href="{{ t.video }}">Video</a>.{% endif %}</span></li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
<p class="more"><a href="{{ research }}#talks">All talks</a></p>
{% endcall %}



{% call section("Contact", "contact") %}
<p class="lead"><a href="mailto:{{ profile.email }}">{{ profile.email }}</a></p>
{% endcall %}
